<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; History by century</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The 11th century</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on the 1000s: the states, events and people of the century. Use its page to find the answers.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/centuries/11th-century">Open the century page &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><p class="ws-how">Each number marks the capital or seat of a state that existed in 1050 CE. Write its name from the word bank on the line with the same number.</p><figure class="ws-mapfig"><svg class="map map-world ws-map" viewBox="0 0 10764 5665" role="img" aria-label="Map: 8 numbered states of the world in 1050 CE"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><g class="ws-pins"><g><circle cx="5709" cy="970" r="183"/><text x="5709" y="1047" font-size="220">1</text></g><g><circle cx="6134" cy="1224" r="183"/><text x="6134" y="1301" font-size="220">2</text></g><g><circle cx="7866" cy="1006" r="183"/><text x="7866" y="1083" font-size="220">3</text></g><g><circle cx="6748" cy="1217" r="183"/><text x="6748" y="1293" font-size="220">4</text></g><g><circle cx="4970" cy="663" r="183"/><text x="4970" y="740" font-size="220">5</text></g><g><circle cx="7846" cy="1933" r="183"/><text x="7846" y="2010" font-size="220">6</text></g><g><circle cx="4799" cy="1289" r="183"/><text x="4799" y="1366" font-size="220">7</text></g><g><circle cx="7088" cy="1770" r="183"/><text x="7088" y="1847" font-size="220">8</text></g></g></svg><figcaption>The world in 1050 CE</figcaption></figure><p class="ws-bank"><b>Word bank:</b> Almoravid Empire &middot; Liao dynasty &middot; Kingdom of England &middot; Ghaznavid Empire &middot; Khmer Empire &middot; Abbasid Caliphate &middot; Byzantine Empire &middot; Western Chalukya Empire</p><ol class="ws-blanks"><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li><li><span class="ws-line1"></span></li></ol></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the events from 1 (earliest) to 6 (latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Sagrajas</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Manzikert</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Tamarón</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Dandanaqan</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Hastings</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>First Crusade</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right dates next to each person. Look them up in the encyclopedia.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Mahmud of Ghazni</li><li>William the Conqueror</li><li>Alfonso VI of Castile</li><li>Yaroslav the Wise</li><li>Alp Arslan</li><li>Harold Godwinson</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 1022–1066</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 978–1054</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 1029–1072</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 1040–1109</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>c. 1028–1087</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>971–1030</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>In the 1000s, 209 recorded states were founded and 135 came to an end. Choose one of each from the century page. What happened to them?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The great powers of the age included the Byzantine Empire, the Abbasid Caliphate and the Liao dynasty. Choose one: what made it strong in these hundred years, and what threatened it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one event from the list and one person. How might they be connected? Use the encyclopedia to find out.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>If you could visit one place in the 11th century, where would you go, and what would you hope to see?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/centuries/11th-century. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The 11th century</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Name the states on the map</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Byzantine Empire <span>330 CE – 1453 CE</span></li><li>Abbasid Caliphate <span>750 CE – 1517 CE</span></li><li>Liao dynasty <span>916 CE – 1125 CE</span></li><li>Ghaznavid Empire <span>977 CE – 1186 CE</span></li><li>Kingdom of England <span>927 CE – 1707 CE</span></li><li>Khmer Empire <span>802 CE – 1431 CE</span></li><li>Almoravid Empire <span>1040 CE – 1147 CE</span></li><li>Western Chalukya Empire <span>973 CE – 1189 CE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Put the events in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Battle of Tamarón <span>1037</span></li><li>Battle of Dandanaqan <span>1040</span></li><li>Battle of Hastings <span>1066</span></li><li>Battle of Manzikert <span>1071</span></li><li>Battle of Sagrajas <span>1086</span></li><li>First Crusade <span>captured Jerusalem 1099</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Match the people to their dates</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Mahmud of Ghazni <span>6: 971–1030</span></li><li>William the Conqueror <span>5: c. 1028–1087</span></li><li>Alfonso VI of Castile <span>4: c. 1040–1109</span></li><li>Yaroslav the Wise <span>2: c. 978–1054</span></li><li>Alp Arslan <span>3: c. 1029–1072</span></li><li>Harold Godwinson <span>1: c. 1022–1066</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">4</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers name states, people and events from the century page.</p></section></div></details>
